    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n**Mode line (bottom), new `sp-modeline-parts` shared by `sp-lambda-modeline` and `sp-prot-modeline`**\n- Order: window number, major mode (nerd-icons, boxed), word count (text buffers) or line:column (code), keycast (key boxed, command next to it, last command kept, fixed width), minor-mode count (button: click for menu, right-click for `describe-mode`). Tags and branch stay at the right.\n- Boxes are as tall as the mode line and take `sp-themes` accent colours (font-lock colours with other themes). Which segments are boxed, their order, hiding in narrow windows and a Doom-style bar are options (`sp-modeline-parts-boxed`, `-left`, `-right`, `-narrow-width`, `-bar`).\n- Lambda uses the layout only in text and prog buffers (via advice on `lambda-line-compose`); Prot loses its own buffer-name, major-mode, minor-modes and keycast segments in favour of the shared ones.\n\n**Header line (`sp-nano-style`)**: buffer name (Org `#+title:`, in `org-document-title` face) and an `hh:mm` clock at the right (Prot's `display-time` settings; clock removed from the mode line). New options `sp-nano-style-divider-opacity`, `-divider-color`, `-header-divider`, and a doc section on making the lines fainter.\n\n**`sp-mini-frame`**: `M-x` is centred like every other prompt. From nano only the text styling and boxes: inverted bold prompt with a box, one-pixel border, and a dotted line (`sp-mini-frame-divider-char`) under the input in the divider colour. Dimming now also applies to `sp-select-note`, `sp-insert-note` and `sp-collec-query-select-note` (`sp-mini-frame-dim-functions`).\n\n**Interpretations:** \"dotted line\" in the mode line is not possible with an overline, so it is a fainter solid line; the dotted row is only under `M-x`. \"Otherwise\" in the mini-frame item was read as \"use the same divider style\". Window number box is on by default.\n\n**Not tested** (nothing run, no Emacs in the container; `.el` files only paren-checked): keycast anchor inside lambda-line, `:position t` underline under the header, the dotted line vs Vertico's candidate overlay (`sp-mini-frame-divider-priority`), word-count caching, window number from `selected-window`, accent colours, `mini-frame-internal-border-color`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01MfEFZ7KDkwwcifErLfjf4X)_",
